{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The researchers created a corpus of 5,000 Reddit posts annotated with levels of dogmatism.","source_span":"we have created a corpus of 5,000 Reddit posts annotated with levels of dogmatism"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The training dataset was built by randomly sampling 1000 posts each from the subreddits politics, business, science, and AskReddit, plus 1000 additional posts from the Reddit frontpage.","source_span":"we have randomly sampled 1000 posts each from the subreddits politics, business, science, and AskReddit, and 1000 additional posts from the Reddit frontpage"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"All sampled posts appeared on Reddit between January 2007 and March 2015.","source_span":"All posts in our sample appeared between January 2007 and March 2015"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"To control for length effects, sampled posts contained between 300 and 400 characters.","source_span":"contain between 300 and 400 characters"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The sampling resulted in a total training dataset of 5000 posts.","source_span":"This results in a total training dataset of 5000 posts."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The Reddit dataset was labeled using crowdworkers on Amazon Mechanical Turk (AMT).","source_span":"We labeled the Reddit dataset using crowdworkers on Amazon Mechanical Turk (AMT)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"Crowdworkers rated levels of dogmatism on a 5-point Likert scale.","source_span":"we asked crowdworkers to rate levels of dogmatism on a 5-point Likert scale"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The annotation task was restricted to Masters workers on AMT to ensure quality.","source_span":"we restricted the task to Masters workers and provided examples corresponding to each point on the scale"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"The paper poses four research questions (R1-R4): what topics attract the highest dogmatism, how dogmatic beliefs cluster, how dogmatism influences conversation, and how other user behaviors relate to dogmatism.","source_span":"R1: What kinds of topics (e.g., guns, LGBT) attract the highest levels of dogmatism?"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","statement":"After training on the 5,000 annotated posts, the model was used to analyze millions of other Reddit posts to answer the research questions.","source_span":"Our model is trained on only 5,000 annotated posts, but once trained, we use it to analyze millions of other Reddit posts to answer our research questions."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[0,4],"question":"How many Reddit posts make up the corpus annotated with dogmatism levels in this study?","answer":"The corpus consists of 5,000 Reddit posts annotated with levels of dogmatism, forming the total training dataset."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[1],"question":"Which subreddits were sampled to build the dogmatism training dataset, and how many posts came from each?","answer":"1000 posts each were sampled from politics, business, science, and AskReddit, plus 1000 additional posts from the Reddit frontpage."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What time period do the sampled Reddit posts in the dogmatism corpus span?","answer":"All posts in the sample appeared between January 2007 and March 2015."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What character-length constraint was applied when sampling Reddit posts for the dogmatism dataset?","answer":"To control for length effects, sampled posts were required to contain between 300 and 400 characters."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[5,6,7],"question":"How was the dogmatism annotation task set up, including platform, rating scale, and worker qualifications?","answer":"Crowdworkers on Amazon Mechanical Turk rated dogmatism on a 5-point Likert scale, and the task was restricted to Masters workers with examples provided for each scale point."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0076","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What are the four research questions (R1-R4) the dogmatism model is used to answer?","answer":"They ask which topics attract the highest levels of dogmatism, how dogmatic beliefs cluster, how dogmatism influences a conversation, and how other user behaviors relate to dogmatism."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"The study uses two taxonomies, SNOMED-CT and MeSH, obtained via the UMLS Metathesaurus version 2016AA.","source_span":"We obtain SNOMED–CT and MeSH via the Unified Medical Language System (UMLS) Metathesaurus (version 2016AA)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"The UMLS Metathesaurus contains approximately 2 million biomedical and clinical concepts integrated from over 150 different terminologies.","source_span":"The Metathesaurus contains approximately 2 million biomedical and clinical concepts from over 150 different terminologies"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"Concepts in the Metathesaurus are connected largely by two types of hierarchical relations: parent/child (PAR/CHD) and broader/narrower (RB/RN).","source_span":"Concepts in the Metathesaurus are connected largely by two types of hierarchical relations: INLINEFORM0 / INLINEFORM1 (PAR/CHD) and INLINEFORM2 / INLINEFORM3 (RB/RN)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"Semantic similarity measures can be classified into three broad categories: path-based, feature-based, and information content (IC).","source_span":"Measures of semantic similarity can be classified into three broad categories : path–based, feature–based and information content (IC)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"Rada et al. (1989) introduced the Conceptual Distance measure, defined as the length of the shortest path between two concepts in the MeSH hierarchy using broader-than (RB) and narrower-than (RN) relations.","source_span":"RadaMBB89 introduce the Conceptual Distance measure. This measure is simply the length of the shortest path between two concepts ( INLINEFORM0 and INLINEFORM1 ) in the MeSH hierarchy."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"CaviedesC04 extended the Conceptual Distance measure to use parent (PAR) and child (CHD) relations.","source_span":"CaviedesC04 extends this measure to use parent (PAR) and child (CHD) relations."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"Wu and Palmer (1994) introduced a correction to the shortest-path similarity measure that incorporates the depth of the two concepts and the depth of their Least Common Subsumer (LCS): similarity is twice the LCS depth divided by the product of the individual concepts' depths.","source_span":"similarity is twice the depth of the two concept's LCS divided by the product of the depths of the individual concepts"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","statement":"The method was evaluated on two datasets: one annotated for both similarity and relatedness, and another annotated for relatedness by two types of experts, medical doctors and medical coders.","source_span":"One has been annotated for both similarity and relatedness, and the other has been annotated for relatedness by two different types of experts (medical doctors and medical coders)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[0,1],"question":"Which two taxonomies does this paper use for semantic similarity, and where were they obtained from?","answer":"The paper uses SNOMED-CT and MeSH, both obtained via the UMLS Metathesaurus, version 2016AA."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How many biomedical and clinical concepts does the UMLS Metathesaurus contain, and from how many terminologies were they integrated?","answer":"The Metathesaurus contains approximately 2 million biomedical and clinical concepts, integrated from over 150 different terminologies."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What are the three broad categories used to classify semantic similarity measures in this paper?","answer":"Semantic similarity measures are classified as path-based, feature-based, or information content (IC) based."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What is the Conceptual Distance measure introduced by Rada et al. (1989) based on?","answer":"It is simply the length of the shortest path between two concepts in the MeSH hierarchy, using broader-than (RB) and narrower-than (RN) relations."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[6],"question":"How does the Wu and Palmer (1994) similarity measure correct for differences in concept specificity?","answer":"It uses the depth of the two concepts' Least Common Subsumer (LCS): similarity equals twice the LCS depth divided by the product of the depths of the individual concepts."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0077","fact_refs":[7],"question":"How were the two evaluation datasets used in this study annotated?","answer":"One dataset was annotated for both similarity and relatedness, while the other was annotated for relatedness by two types of experts: medical doctors and medical coders."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0078","statement":"The classifier categorizes the stance of each tweet in a rumourous conversation as supporting, denying, or questioning the rumour.","source_span":"classify the stance expressed in each individual tweet in a rumourous conversation as either supporting, denying or questioning the rumour"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0078","statement":"The classifier is based on Gaussian Processes combined with multi-task learning.","source_span":"we set out to develop an automated, supervised classifier that uses multi-task learning to classify the stance"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0078","statement":"The approach was tested on two datasets with very different characteristics and varying distributions of stances.","source_span":"exploring its effectiveness on two datasets with very different characteristics and varying distributions of stances"}
